# Worktree directories created by `git worktree add`. Each
# per-machine, per-branch, with its own .git pointer; never
# committed.
.worktrees/

# time-honesty-storage obligation storage-paths-declared:
# per-worktree runtime data; never committed, never uploaded.
.local
decisions/execution-logs.jsonl
scripts/__pycache__/

# Playwright MCP browser session artifacts (local profile,
# screenshots, traces). Regenerated on every browser run.
.playwright-mcp/

# The historical /doc/ directory was merged into /docs/ as
# of commit 65d3015's follow-up. Any stray file dropped into
# /doc/ by a future tool is a mistake; the canonical location
# for audits, historical notes, and upstream-bug records is
# /docs/.
/doc/

# The attestation store is GENERATED evidence, not a committed
# artefact. It is produced by scripts/sign-store.sh (and by CI,
# which regenerates it and uploads it as a build artefact), it is
# excluded from every materials digest, and committing it puts
# ~890 generated files into every diff that touches a decision.
# Measured over the last 60 commits on main: 12337 of 12556 file
# touches (98.3%) were under attestations/, and 33 of those 60
# commits touched nothing else at all.
#
# The pattern is ROOT-ANCHORED on purpose. An unanchored
# `attestations/` would also match any directory of that name
# deeper in the tree, and a fixture store under
# tests/fixtures/ is a COMMITTED artefact: a rule that swallowed it
# would silently drop a fixture from version control.
#
# Decision: decisions/store-not-committed-2026-10.yaml.
/attestations/

# Two named scratch decisions, kept as a name-exact list on purpose.
# They were once scaffolded by the tests/cli/adopt.t and
# `mathc import-adr --write` flows; since the 3.4 path resolver those
# flows write into a bwrap tmpdir's `.math-coding/decisions/`, and
# neither name was ever tracked, so no current fixture produces them.
# They stay listed because the name is unambiguous: a decision called
# `1-foo` cannot be mistaken for a real commitment.
#
# Do NOT widen this into a pattern. `mathc import-adr --write` names its
# output after the ADR title, keeping the ADR number as a prefix only
# when the source file was numerically prefixed -- so `0001-format.md`
# yields `1-use-ocamlformat-for-source-formatting.yaml` and
# `adr-null-safety.md` yields `use-null-safety-checks.yaml`. Both show
# up as untracked, so these two rules do not cover them. There is
# nothing to widen them to: `mathc new-decision foo` and a real decision
# `foo` produce byte-identical filenames, so no pattern can separate
# scratch from committed. Measured against the 233 tracked decisions,
# `decisions/*use*.yaml` already swallows
# `auto-update-per-user-skill-impl-pending.yaml` and
# `decisions/[0-9]*-*.yaml` already swallows `3-2-cli-catalog.yaml`;
# `decisions/use-*.yaml` is clean today but swallows the entirely
# plausible `use-postgresql-for-storage.yaml`. A wrong guess here drops
# a real commitment out of version control silently, which is worse
# than the red test it would prevent.
#
# To create a decision without touching this corpus, point the resolver
# elsewhere: `MATH_CODING_DECISIONS_DIR=scratch-decisions mathc
# import-adr ... --write` writes there and leaves decisions/ untouched
# (the env-var branch of lib/path_config.ml; covered by
# tests/cli/env-var-resolver.t).
decisions/1-foo.yaml
decisions/1-use-postgresql.yaml

# `scripts/render-svgs.sh` emits PNG snapshots of every
# assets/*.svg here. The snapshots are visual-verification
# scratch — regenerated on every render — and should never
# be committed.
assets/_renders/
tools/winget/scripts/__pycache__/
.dev/
.work/

# Cram fixtures that log to the repo root (tests/cli/adopt-real-arc42.t
# and init-*): scratch output, not committed artefacts.
adopt.log
init.log

# Scratch prefix created by hermetic cram fixtures that cd into the
# checkout (attest-batch-*). Empty dirs are invisible to git; the
# prefix stays out of history either way.
.test-math-coding/
sign-store-sweep.log
